[0.434719, "o", "Stado — policy-controlled queue and compute control plane.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mUsage:\u001b[0m \u001b[1mstado\u001b[0m [COMMAND]\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mCommands:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1mcapabilities\u001b[0m          List Stado capability families, variants, providers and active selections\r\n  \u001b[1moverview\u001b[0m              One operator snapshot: jobs, active workers, quota, budgets, burn and credits\r\n  \u001b[1mblast-radius\u001b[0m          Inventory a dependency's live resources, auth, consumers, storage, and DR coverage\r\n  \u001b[1mresources\u001b[0m             Inventory, plan, execute, verify, and restore resource operations\r\n  \u001b[1moptimize\u001b[0m              Inspect and control autonomous placement and resource reconciliation\r\n  \u001b[1mbilling\u001b[0m               Inspect or refresh cross-cloud costs, grants, burn, and credit balances\r\n  \u001b[1mazure\u001b[0m                 Authenticate an Azure operator and repair the Stado RBAC contract\r\n  \u001b[1mcloudflare\u001b[0m            Configure Cloudflare Tunnel ingress and DNS through Stado-held credentials\r\n  \u001b[1mmail\u001b[0m                  Search and d"]
[0.43473, "o", "eterministically analyze Gmail messages without modifying them\r\n  \u001b[1mdisk-cleanup\u001b[0m          Run registry-authorized cleanup for this local target\r\n  \u001b[1minstall-disk-cleanup\u001b[0m  Install the registry-controlled cleanup watch on this Mac\r\n  \u001b[1mmachine\u001b[0m               Stable JSON machine interface\r\n  \u001b[1msubmit\u001b[0m                Submit a job (or batch) to the queue\r\n  \u001b[1mstatus\u001b[0m                Show job status\r\n  \u001b[1mresults\u001b[0m               Download job results\r\n  \u001b[1mcancel\u001b[0m                Cancel a queued or running job\r\n  \u001b[1mjob\u001b[0m                   Rerun or watch one job\r\n  \u001b[1magent\u001b[0m                 Run local GPU agent. Polls queue, respects Vast.ai renters\r\n  \u001b[1mcoordinator\u001b[0m           Run the provider-neutral scheduling tick locally\r\n  \u001b[1mdashboard\u001b[0m             Run the Stado API listener for the wisent-compute queue\r\n  \u001b[1mquota\u001b[0m                 GPU quota inspection and increase requests across WC_PROVIDERS\r\n  \u001b[1mprofiles\u001b[0m              List available submit profiles, or "]
[0.43474, "o", "show one profile's JSON\r\n  \u001b[1mconfig\u001b[0m                Inspect or change stado configuration: show | validate | init | set\r\n  \u001b[1martifact\u001b[0m              Publish and consume immutable, versioned artifacts\r\n  \u001b[1mrelease\u001b[0m               Build once, sign, promote, roll out, and roll back product releases\r\n  \u001b[1mschedule\u001b[0m              Manage recurring (cron) jobs — submit a command on a cron schedule\r\n  \u001b[1mcost\u001b[0m                  Per-job and per-batch cost reporting from observed wall-times\r\n  \u001b[1mregistry\u001b[0m              Manage the canonical compute-target registry in configured Stado storage\r\n  \u001b[1mbuilds\u001b[0m                Manage native build recipes: poll a repo, build on new commits\r\n  \u001b[1mfleet\u001b[0m                 Add machines to the fleet, group them, hold their SSH keys, and diagnose the workers: enroll, join/approve, key, doctor\r\n  \u001b[1midentity\u001b[0m              Which host holds which identity, and whether that is still true\r\n  \u001b[1mhost\u001b[0m                  Manage operating-system resource"]
[0.434745, "o", "s on registry hosts\r\n  \u001b[1mbootstrap\u001b[0m             Provision wisent-compute services persistently across reboots\r\n  \u001b[1mvast\u001b[0m                  Vast.ai marketplace host-listing (rent our idle GPU)\r\n  \u001b[1minstances\u001b[0m             Inspect and reap live agent VMs across the configured cloud providers\r\n  \u001b[1mrecovery\u001b[0m              Transactional outage recovery: fence, migrate, verify, and cut over\r\n  \u001b[1mstorage\u001b[0m               Move queue state between storage backends (billing-outage migration)\r\n  \u001b[1mcredentials\u001b[0m           Read, migrate, and manage application credentials in the selected store [alias: secrets]\r\n  \u001b[1mqueue\u001b[0m                 Maintenance mode: pause/resume dispatching, and drain the fleet\r\n  \u001b[1malerts\u001b[0m                Show which alert channels resolve, and page them on purpose\r\n  \u001b[1mservice\u001b[0m               Manage the services registry hosts run: list, status, restart, adopt, retire, deploy, logs, env\r\n  \u001b[1mplacement\u001b[0m             Atomically relocate a declared service grou"]
[0.434759, "o", "p between registered hosts\r\n  \u001b[1mresolver\u001b[0m              Resolve logical services and run the local Stado data plane\r\n  \u001b[1minference\u001b[0m             Plan, deploy, route and operate local OpenAI-compatible inference\r\n  \u001b[1mstream\u001b[0m                Provision and operate an interactive display session on a host, and stream it to a client (Moonlight): the way to use a fleet GPU interactively, since a board cannot be borrowed over a network\r\n  \u001b[1mdoctor\u001b[0m                Ordered deployment preflight: config, storage, provider auth, quota, release channel, agent template, VM identity, registry, queue pause state and alert channels. Exits non-zero if any check FAILs\r\n  \u001b[1mhelp\u001b[0m                  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mOptions:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m-h\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--help\u001b[0m     Print help\r\n  \u001b[1m-V\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--version\u001b[0m  Print version\r\n"]
